  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T01:30:05.052Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, a self-employed individual is required to file an annual income tax return. This obligation is outlined in Section 51 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\n- **NIRC Section 51**: This section mandates that every individual, including self-employed persons, must file an income tax return for income derived from all sources.\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51 of the NIRC specifies that individuals who are Filipino citizens residing in the Philippines, as well as those residing outside the Philippines on income sourced within the country, are required to file an income tax return. This includes self-employed individuals who earn income from their business activities.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor self-employed individuals, this means they must prepare and submit their income tax returns annually, detailing their income and expenses, and pay any taxes due. The filing deadline is typically on or before April 15 of the following year, covering the income for the preceding taxable year. Failure to file can result in penalties and interest on unpaid taxes.",
